I’m going to replace `submission.py` with a hybrid implementation now: PyTorch does the high-throughput GEMMs, Triton fuses the sigmoid/mask/layout transform before the contraction and fuses the hidden LayerNorm/gate after it. That keeps the custom kernels focused on memory layout and elementwise work where they are useful.
